{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791692327,"nonce":"SOFK+Ahoyww7OYPkfxoTBdjcBxw=","message":"Decision: jobhunter upgrade builds localhost/jobhunter:\u003ccommit\u003e before stopping anything, then stops timers, waits for running jobhunter-ctr-* services (--wait, default 30m), takes the run lock non-blocking, and only then stops the console. A wait timeout or a held lock starts the timers again and exits 1 with nothing changed. Reason: the units use :current so a new tag changes nothing; a failed build or a long nightly run should not leave the console down. From the console stop on, any failure leaves console and timers stopped and prints the rollback.","files":null}]}